# SRC/ is ~25G (WRF alone is ~18G, dominated by one restart file, plus large
# GROMACS/NAMD/OpenFOAM input data and binaries). Too large for GitHub and
# mostly data, not code -- backed up separately and downloaded before first
# run. See README.md for the download/restore instructions.
SRC/

# Nightly cron output: verification/submission logs, per-date node lists,
# debug reports, generated charts. Regenerated fresh on every run, grows
# without bound, and isn't needed to run the setup on a new system -- not
# source code, so not version-controlled. Back these up separately (outside
# git) if historical run data itself needs preserving.
LOGS/
CRON/Verification/LOGS/
CRON/Verification/cron-job-verification-logs/
CRON/Jobsubmission/cron-job-submission-logs/
CRON/graph/*.png

# Per-run verification state files: each verify-results.sh rm's and
# regenerates these at the start of every run (see e.g.
# gromacs-verify-results.sh's cleanup block) -- pure runtime state, not
# something to commit. Same pattern also appears one level deeper under
# SCRIPTS/debug/faulti-node-detection/{1N,2N}/ (an older, standalone
# fault-detection tool with its own copies of the same verify scripts), so
# matched by filename at any depth rather than one fixed path.
**/SuccesfullJobIDs
**/FailedJobIDs
**/FileNotExistsJobIDs
**/ResultOutOffRengeJobIDs

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
